WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.020
Every growing services business reaches a moment

2
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.808
when the tools that got it started can't keep up with where it's going.

3
00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:12.228
So before you choose a CRM, run five checks:

4
00:00:12.228 --> 00:00:20.331
your data model, the cost of growing, operations after the sale, governance and control, and your AI and data foundation.

5
00:00:21.281 --> 00:00:23.421
If you run a services business,

6
00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:29.121
from home services, waste and water to construction, staffing, legal and consulting,

7
00:00:29.121 --> 00:00:31.869
your business doesn't run on deals alone.

8
00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:35.129
It runs on projects, work orders, job orders and matters,

9
00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:40.456
through acquisitions, crews in the field, and the systems that bill it all.

10
00:00:40.456 --> 00:00:42.910
Plenty of tools are easy to start.

11
00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:46.427
Salesforce is built to scale. Here's the proof.

12
00:00:46.877 --> 00:00:49.125
Check one: your data model.

13
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:56.765
Salesforce lets you build your real business: projects, work orders, job orders, matters and the relationships between them,

14
00:00:56.765 --> 00:01:00.591
with account hierarchies for every brand you acquire.

15
00:01:00.591 --> 00:01:04.531
HubSpot falls short. It centers on contacts, companies and deals.

16
00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:10.610
Custom objects sit in its top tier, and a company can have just one parent.

17
00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.545
Check two: the cost of growing.

18
00:01:13.545 --> 00:01:17.845
Salesforce is one platform you can start small on and grow into,

19
00:01:17.845 --> 00:01:20.823
with new capabilities on the same foundation.

20
00:01:20.823 --> 00:01:26.503
With HubSpot, growth can mean another hub, a higher tier, and another onboarding fee.

21
00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:31.666
Marketing contacts are billed in tiers, and going over is billed immediately.

22
00:01:32.316 --> 00:01:35.245
Check three: operations after the sale.

23
00:01:35.245 --> 00:01:43.636
Salesforce runs the whole path, from quote and approval to contract, handoff, field work, billing and service, on one platform.

24
00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:51.676
One multi-location home services company now has Agentforce handling 100% of its after-hours calls.

25
00:01:51.676 --> 00:01:54.616
HubSpot is strongest at the front of the funnel.

26
00:01:54.616 --> 00:02:02.432
It doesn't offer native field service, so dispatch and delivery mean separate apps, and its voice agent is still in beta.

27
00:02:03.182 --> 00:02:05.689
Check four: governance and control.

28
00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:12.989
Salesforce gives you record-level security, role hierarchies, and approval flows across every business unit,

29
00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:17.128
with sandboxes to test every change before it goes live.

30
00:02:17.128 --> 00:02:23.409
In HubSpot, field-level permissions sit in its top tier, and you get one standard sandbox.

31
00:02:24.059 --> 00:02:27.211
Check five: your AI and data foundation.

32
00:02:27.211 --> 00:02:34.051
Agentforce works on all your data, connected through Data 360, MuleSoft and Zero Copy,

33
00:02:34.051 --> 00:02:39.335
and every agent is tested, versioned and governed by the Einstein Trust Layer.

34
00:02:39.335 --> 00:02:44.175
HubSpot's AI credits reset every month, agents pause when they run out,

35
00:02:44.175 --> 00:02:48.766
and its agent builder doesn't document version history or rollback.

36
00:02:49.516 --> 00:02:52.972
That's the difference between a CRM and a platform.

37
00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:56.229
Salesforce is built for the agentic enterprise.

38
00:02:56.229 --> 00:02:59.349
Your data comes together in Data 360.

39
00:02:59.349 --> 00:03:02.789
Sales, service and field run on one platform.

40
00:03:02.789 --> 00:03:03.769
Agentforce does real work.

41
00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:07.596
Slack is where your teams and agents meet.

42
00:03:07.596 --> 00:03:09.456
And it's open by design:

43
00:03:09.456 --> 00:03:14.618
it connects to your ERP, your data warehouse, and AI models like Claude.

44
00:03:15.368 --> 00:03:16.870
And it pays off.

45
00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:25.634
In engineering, construction and real estate, 99% achieved positive ROI, with 60% ROI achieved.

46
00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:30.789
In professional services, 97% achieved positive ROI.

47
00:03:30.789 --> 00:03:40.966
Field service teams report a 38% improvement in customer satisfaction, and customer service teams respond 35% faster.

48
00:03:40.966 --> 00:03:46.152
From staffing to legal services to home services, the results follow the work.

49
00:03:47.702 --> 00:03:52.134
So before you choose, ask HubSpot to prove it, live, with your data.

50
00:03:52.134 --> 00:03:55.220
Can it build your real objects, and how they connect?

51
00:03:55.220 --> 00:04:00.590
Can it run quote to delivery, billing and service in one system, without separate apps?

52
00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:05.048
Can its AI work on data from outside the CRM, with guardrails?

53
00:04:05.048 --> 00:04:09.069
Ask for a proof of concept on the first two. Then ask us.

54
00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:14.216
Salesforce will show you all three, live, on your data, because we can prove it.

55
00:04:14.216 --> 00:04:17.721
Easy to start is good. Built to scale is better.

56
00:04:17.721 --> 00:04:20.315
Talk to your Salesforce account team.
